      "text": "To determine the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to use the information given about his walk. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we know that walking the length 25 times will cover a distance of 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 25l = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( l \\), we get:\n\\[ l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, we know that walking the perimeter 10 times will also cover a distance of 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[ P = 2l + 2w \\]\nSo, walking the perimeter 10 times means:\n\\[ 10P = 1000 \\]\nSubstituting the expression for \\( P \\), we get:\n\\[ 10(2l + 2w) = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 2l + 2w = 100 \\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[ l + w = 50 \\]\nSince we already know \\( l = 40 \\), we can substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[ 40 + w = 50 \\]\nSolving for \\( w \\), we get:\n\\[ w = 50 - 40 = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have the length \\( l = 40 \\) meters and the width \\( w = 10 \\) meters, we can find the area \\( A \\) of the backyard using the formula for the area of a rectangle:\n\\[ A = l \\times w = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is:\n\\[ \\boxed{400} \\]",
