      "text": "First, let's find the perimeter of Mateen's backyard. Since he needs to walk the perimeter 10 times to cover a kilometer, the distance around the backyard is:\n1 kilometer / 10 times = 1000 meters / 10 = 100 meters\n\nNow, let's denote the length of the backyard as \\( L \\) and the width as \\( W \\). The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by the formula:\n\\[ P = 2L + 2W \\]\nWe know that \\( P = 100 \\) meters, so:\n\\[ 100 = 2L + 2W \\]\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\\[ 50 = L + W \\]\n\\[ L = 50 - W \\]\n\nNext, we use the information that Mateen walks the length 25 times to cover a kilometer:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( L \\), we get:\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\]\nNow we substitute \\( L = 40 \\) back into the equation \\( L = 50 - W \\):\n\\[ 40 = 50 - W \\]\n\\[ W = 50 - 40 \\]\n\\[ W = 10 \\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of the backyard is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = L \\times W \\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\\[ A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\]\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
