      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the dimensions of Mateen's backyard and then calculate its area. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the dimensions of the backyard\n\nWe are given two pieces of information:\n1. Mateen must walk the length 25 times to cover 1 kilometer (1000 meters).\n2. Mateen must walk the perimeter 10 times to cover 1 kilometer (1000 meters).\n\nLet's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\n#### Using the length:\n- Walking the length 25 times means the total distance walked is:\n  \\[\n  25L = 1000 \\text{ meters}\n  \\]\n- Solving for \\( L \\):\n  \\[\n  L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n  \\]\n\n#### Using the perimeter:\n- The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n  \\[\n  P = 2L + 2W\n  \\]\n- Walking the perimeter 10 times means the total distance walked is:\n  \\[\n  10P = 1000 \\text{ meters}\n  \\]\n- Substituting \\( P = 2L + 2W \\):\n  \\[\n  10(2L + 2W) = 1000\n  \\]\n- Simplifying:\n  \\[\n  20L + 20W = 1000\n  \\]\n- Dividing the entire equation by 20:\n  \\[\n  L + W = 50\n  \\]\n\n#### Using the length \\( L = 40 \\) meters:\n- Substitute \\( L = 40 \\) into the equation \\( L + W = 50 \\):\n  \\[\n  40 + W = 50\n  \\]\n- Solving for \\( W \\):\n  \\[\n  W = 50 - 40 = 10 \\text{ meters}\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the area of the backyard\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nA = L \\times W\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\\[\nA = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{400}\n\\]",
