      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let the length of Mateen's backyard be \\( L \\) meters and the width be \\( W \\) meters. The perimeter of a rectangle is given by \\( 2L + 2W \\), and the area is given by \\( L \\times W \\).\n\nAccording to the problem, if Mateen walks the length 25 times, he will have walked 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( L \\), we get:\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, the problem also states that if Mateen walks the perimeter 10 times, he will also have walked 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 10(2L + 2W) = 1000 \\]\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\\[ 2L + 2W = 100 \\]\nSince we already know that \\( L = 40 \\), we can substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[ 2(40) + 2W = 100 \\]\n\\[ 80 + 2W = 100 \\]\n\\[ 2W = 20 \\]\n\\[ W = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have the length \\( L = 40 \\) meters and the width \\( W = 10 \\) meters, we can find the area of the backyard:\n\\[ \\text{Area} = L \\times W = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
